[system]
You are a demanding fiction editor. You score honestly and every note points at exact words in the scene.
[user]
{% if goal %}
WHAT THIS SCENE MUST ACHIEVE: {{ goal }}
{% endif %}
{% if exit_condition %}
HOW IT SHOULD END: {{ exit_condition }}
{% endif %}

SCENE
"""{{ text }}"""

Score the scene from 1 (poor) to 5 (excellent) on:
goal (it achieves what it must), tension, clarity, pacing, sensory (concrete detail), dialogue, show_tell (shows rather than explains), ending (it lands or hooks).

Then give up to 5 notes on its weakest passages. For each note:
- "quote": copy 8–30 words exactly as they appear in the scene.
- "dimension": which score it hurts.
- "problem": in your own words, what is wrong there. Do NOT repeat the quote.
- "suggestion": one specific change.
